  "reasoning": "The claim is scientifically accurate and widely documented. Data from the Lunar Laser Ranging experiment—which bounces lasers off retroreflectors left on the Moon by Apollo missions—has precisely measured that the Moon recedes from Earth at an average rate of approximately 3.78 to 3.8 centimeters (about 1.5 inches) per year. This gradual recession occurs because tidal friction created by the Moon's pull on Earth's oceans slows Earth's rotation and transfers angular momentum into the Moon's orbit, pushing it slowly outward.",
